jobs.description:
As an operator, you'll work in a two-shift system and be responsible for part of the production process. By operating the machines, your goal is to meet production demand with the desired quality. Independently operate, monitor, and maintain the production line;

- Identify and resolve machine malfunctions;
- Set up machines based on the production schedule;
- Monitor product quality using various measuring instruments;
- Ensure timely machine maintenance in consultation with your manager and the Technical Department;
- Contribute to structural improvement opportunities;
- Coordinating workflows in consultation with your manager.

- A technical background or extensive experience in production technology is a plus;
- You are willing to work night shifts;
- You have technical knowledge and enjoy brainstorming;
- You are a natural at solution-oriented error analysis;
- You are a precision engineer;
- You have knowledge of and experience with production processes;
- You are decisive, practical, and enjoy working in a team.
- A driving license (car) is preferred - Maintec arranges transport;
- You can communicate in English at a B1/B2 level.

This is not your average production environment. The organisation you'll be joining is a global frontrunner in identity security, think biometric passports, secure payment cards, facial recognition at international airports, and cryptographic systems used by governments and banks worldwide. 

As Maintenance Engineer, you are the backbone of a smooth-running production floor. When machines go down, you're the one who gets things moving again, but more importantly, you make sure they don't go down in the first place. You combine hands-on technical skill with a structured mindset: you don't just fix problems, you prevent them. 

What you'll be doing

- Keeping production equipment in top condition and reducing unplanned downtime;
- Building and executing preventive maintenance schedules;
- Digging into the root cause of breakdowns — not just patching things up;
- Translating technical findings into clear documentation and practical improvement plans;
- Supporting the roll-out and commissioning of new equipment;
- Working with software controls for production machinery;
- Collaborating with production, management, and other departments on both day-to-day operations and longer-term reliability improvements;
- Monitoring facility and utility systems to ensure a safe working environment.

- An MBO level 4 background in Electrical or Manufacturing Engineering (or equivalent experience);
- A proven track record in a maintenance role within a production environment;
- Good command of English, spoken and written;
- Flexibility to work in shifts and join an on-call rotation;
- Willingness to occasionally travel for training or visits to other sites;
- Strong communication skills and a collaborative attitude.

Please note that we are looking for a part-time colleague (15.2 hours per week).Set next to the picturesque Vondelpark, in the heart of the city, the 396-room Amsterdam Marriott is celebrated for its proximity to significant landmarks such as the Rijksmuseum and Van Gogh Museum, exclusive shopping, vibrant nightlife and high-end restaurants. Opened in 1975 as the first Marriott in Europe, the hotel blends a prime location with contemporary interiors, offering an ideal address for exploring Amsterdam. The hotel also features 11 flexible meeting and event spaces with natural daylight, including our Grand Ballroom and studios. Guests can enjoy premium dining at Midtown Grill, one of Amsterdam's top steak restaurants, as well as Bar TWLV, our cosmopolitan bar offering globally inspired dishes, creative cocktails and a day-to-night atmosphere What are your responsibilities?For our Houseman position, we are looking for a part-time colleague (15.2 hours per week) who is a team player and has an eye for detail when it comes to cleanliness. You will be responsible for the cleanliness on a daily basis in the bar, restaurant and floors. You will also be responsible for the transportation of linen, assisting attendants with garbage and trolleys and handle direct requests from the Front Office colleagues. 

